      "id": 1,
      "text": "French Settlement was founded in 1800 along the Amite River by French, German, and Italian immigrants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Settlement%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 19th century, the village thrived as a commercial hub with cypress sawmills, shingle‑making, animal trapping, farms, and a steamboat port.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Settlement%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Four historic homes—Decareaux, Deslattes, Guitreau, and Lobell—are listed on the National Register of Historic Places in French Settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Settlement%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Creole House Museum in French Settlement showcases local Creole heritage and artifacts from the village’s early days.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.frenchsettlement-la.gov/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "French Louisiana was claimed by France in 1682, a possession that shaped the region for more than a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
